  "decision": "A membership import or a namespace import, as KerML 8.2.3.4.2 and SysML 8.2.2.5.1 both state it.",
  "notes": "Both languages agree on the body. A notational slip in the KerML clause, recorded because it would trip anyone reading it literally: `ImportDeclaration : Import` is followed by its body with no `=`, where every other production, and SysML's statement of this one, has it. Nothing about what parses turns on it.\n\nThere is no Xtext rule of this name; the pilot distributes the two alternatives into its Import rule.\n\nFOR A PARSER AUTHOR: the two alternatives share a leading qualified name and are told apart only after it \u2014 `::*` makes a NamespaceImport, anything else a MembershipImport \u2014 and `[` opens the filter-package form of NamespaceImport.\n\nFILED WITH OMG: the notational slip recorded above is KERML11-108, item 1. It concerns how the rule is written, not what it accepts, so it is recorded as a citation and not as a deviation.",
  "evidence": [
